{
  "body" : "You are designing an expressive monochrome silhouette illustration with an abstract and dynamic visual language.\n\nCONTENT BRIEF\n- Subject: {{subject}}\n- Scene: {{scene}}\n\nSTYLE DIRECTION\n- Genre / medium: Expressionist monochrome illustration\n- Composition: Dynamic overlapping silhouettes with medium-density distribution; balanced negative space and layering\n- Lens / camera: N/A (illustration-specific perspective with implied depth through layering)\n- Lighting: High-contrast interplay of black silhouettes against a textured, light-toned abstract backdrop\n- Color palette and grading: Monochrome palette with dominant black and white tones, subtle grayscale transitions\n- Texture / surface: Visible brushstroke texture and rough gradients in the background\n- Post-processing: None (illustration is raw and textured)\n- Mood: Dramatic, eerie, dynamic, abstract\n- References: Franz Marc's expressionist works, silhouette art traditions, abstract brushstroke techniques\n\nDESIGN RULES\n- Aspect: 2:3 portrait (~1024×1536) suitable for expressive illustration or poster\n- Maintain a clear distinction between foreground silhouettes and textured abstract background\n- Avoid excessive detail in the silhouettes to preserve the bold, graphical style\n\nAVOID\n- No gradients or smooth color transitions beyond subtle brushstroke textures\n- No chromatic elements or vibrant colors\n- No rigid geometric patterns\n- No crowded or overly complex compositions\n- No photographic realism or excessive detail\n\nAdditional constraints: {{extra}}\n\n——————\nSubject: {{subject}}\nScene: {{scene}}\nExtra notes: {{extra}}",
